  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, but I couldn't compile it against the engine or see a render. `node_modules/@aura3d` is empty in this sandbox, so `typecheck` only reports \"Cannot find module '@aura3d/engine'\" and the rest of the file went unchecked. I wrote against the API in `docs/agents/api-signatures.md` and the recipe sources, and I didn't use any option keys that those docs don't mention. I did not use `vite build` or any screenshot. Light intensities, the strip-light orientation and the paint look are untuned guesses.\n\n- **Car:** a stretched-sphere body, a separate black-glass cabin with a red roof cap, and chrome trim (belt strip, window-base ring, front and rear bumper bars). It has four black tires with chrome rims and dark hub caps.\n- **Paint:** `material.physical` in candy red with clearcoat 1 and clearcoat roughness 0.03. About 1,100 tiny metallic flakes, instanced and tinted, sit on the body and roof as the sparkle layer.\n- **Platform:** a glossy dark top disc at 80% opacity, a glowing ring-light band around the edge, and tick marks so the spin is visible. A flipped copy of the car sits under the disc and shows through as the faint mirror image. If `opacity` is ignored, the disc is opaque and the mirror simply disappears.\n- **Lighting:** the `environments.metalStudio` environment at low intensity, plus four long softbox strips (two overhead, two at the sides). A warm key light with shadow, a cool rim light and a faint cool fill complete it. Bloom is on, the background is near-black, and the camera is fixed at a low front-three-quarter angle.\n- **Motion and state:** the `turntable` group is rotated at 20°/s from `performance.now()`. `window.__TASK_STATE__ = { turntableAngleDeg, paintFinish: 'clearcoat' }` is updated every frame from both `app.onFrame` and a `requestAnimationFrame` loop. `__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n- **Top-level await:** I avoided it, so `vite build` works with the default target.\n\n",
